        "id": 1000067
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-02T08:38:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "First because we can implement it after this fix which gets rid of the runtime crashes entirely.\n\nSecond because, I don\u0027t like \"optimistic\" algorithms which can widely alter the timing of `gn gen` times. This will increase its variance, leading to surprising results when benchmarking. Results may change due to a kernel upgrade, or be widely inconsistent between different OSes.\n\nAlso, ideally, I want to get rid of the validations-collecting walks in the Fuchsia build entirely so this wouldn\u0027t be needed at all.\n\nSo I don\u0027t think it\u0027s really worth it, but it can be implemented.\n\nBesides, I have other optimizations to speed up metadata collection deterministically that I intend to push soon, if you\u0027re interested in that.",
      "parentUuid": "4a1654b4_2b904515",
      "revId": "490dacb4e2e53fdc0e09abc40af640af134c9028",
      "serverId": "c360c8e5-7aa8-3905-a7a0-810934766dac"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "18bab73f_6974bb94",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 57,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000067
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-02T08:42:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "And another reason is that I don\u0027t think validations should be part of metadata walks by default. It can only pollute the result with unwanted data, except in rare cases. We tried to prevent this with explicit barriers, but a target doesn\u0027t know all the keys it\u0027s going to be visited with in advance, so this is very fragile (breaks easily when new types of walks are added, and can only be detected by manual review of the results, which is rarely done).\n\nThis is why we have the new `collect_validations_metadata` flag too.",
      "parentUuid": "ecdfe3e0_68f8359b",
      "revId": "490dacb4e2e53fdc0e09abc40af640af134c9028",
      "serverId": "c360c8e5-7aa8-3905-a7a0-810934766dac"
    },
